WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody!

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.801
Here at "The Tonight Show,"
we love songs,

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.501
and we especially
love songs written by

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.801
our audience members
in under an hour.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:10.334
It's time for "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.334
Here we go.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:14.200
-♪ I'm singing a song ♪

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.000
♪ And I'm writing a song ♪

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.133
♪ About another song ♪

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.868
-Oh, welcome to "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:24.133
Before the show, we went through
our great audience

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:27.000
and picked out two people
who said they were musicians.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.167
We gave them each
a made-up song title

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:30.601
and gave them an hour to write

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.067
an original song
based on that title.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.400
This is real.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.367
Here's a shot of them practicing
backstage a minute ago.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.701
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.300
I cannot wait to see
what they come up with,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.534
so let's meet them right now.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:43.000
Come on over, guys.
Welcome to the show. Hey!

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:46.501
Thank you so much.
-Nice to meet you.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:48.934
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:50.067
Let's start with
contestant number 1.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.601
What is your name
and where are you from?

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.634
-I'm Allie Chipkin from
Poughkeepsie, New York.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.434
-No way!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.501
Oh, I got my start over there.
Yeah.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.734
What was the title of the song
you were given?

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.334
-"Too Old to Trick-or-Treat."

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.634
-Ooh!
"Too Old to Trick-or-Treat."

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:06.868
I feel that way.

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.267
What instrument
will you be playing?

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.501
-The guitar.
-Oh, cool.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.868
Alright, why don't you go over
and get ready,

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:14.000
and then I'll introduce you
and give you a good intro.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.467
It's going to be fun.
Don't get nervous.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:16.634
You'll have your shot.
Yeah, it'll be fine.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:18.501
You'll be good.
Yeah, we got this.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:22.067
And now, ladies and gentlemen,
here to perform

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:24.300
the world premiere
of the soon-to-be classic

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.534
"Too Old to Trick-or-Treat,"
it's Allie Chipkin.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:31.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.300
♪♪

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.501
-♪ So what if my hair
is turning gray? ♪

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:44.334
♪ I can still get down with
a Milky Way ♪

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:49.000
♪ And I find the best treatment
for my wrinkles ♪

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.100
♪ Is anything with sprinkles ♪

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.434
♪ Now, I know it's
pretty early in the night ♪

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:03.367
♪ But "Jeopardy!" is at 7:00,

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:06.567
and I don't see well
in dim light ♪

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:11.033
♪ I took off my mask
so I won't overheat ♪

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:16.334
♪ Did you say I'm too old to
trick-or-treat? ♪

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:22.033
♪ Well, you can smell my feet ♪

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:27.567
♪ You don't own this treat ♪

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:33.667
♪ You can smell my feet ♪

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:37.334
♪ I'd even take toothpaste ♪

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:42.734
♪ But I'm not too old to
trick-or-treat ♪

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:45.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:48.033
-That's what I'm talking about.
That's how you do it.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:52.901
Give it up for Allie Chipkin,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:56.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:59.267
Well done. Thank you, pal.
-Thank you.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.767
-Contestant number 2,
what is your name

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.133
and where are you from?

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.767
-My name is Tom McGovern.
I'm from Allentown, New Jersey.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.868
-Hey, Tom!
-Hey!

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:09.300
-Thank you for being here.
-Thanks, dude.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.167
-And tell everyone what
song title was given to you.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:17.934
-The song title was "Let's Avoid
the Weird Guy's House."

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:19.100
-It is Halloween.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.534
"Let's Avoid
the Weird Guy's House."

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.033
And what instrument
will you be playing tonight?

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.133
-I'll be playing piano.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.367
-Alright, Tom,
go over and get ready.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.033
Whenever you're...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:28.634
Come on over.
You can come over here.

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:30.300
That was great.
-Oh, thank you.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:35.300
-Ladies and gentlemen, get ready
for the world premiere of

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.667
"Let's Avoid the Weird
Guy's House" by Tom McGovern.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:41.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:45.334
♪♪

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:47.734
-♪ The sun goes down
on Halloween,

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:50.033
it's time to trick-or-treat ♪

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:52.767
♪ My friends and I
are all dressed up like

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.000
ghosts in fitted sheets ♪

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.534
♪ We go door-to-door to
snag some peanut-butter cups ♪

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:03.934
♪ Then we hear someone shouting,
so we turn to what's up ♪

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.133
♪ Some guy says,
"Hey, come over,

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:09.067
I've got all
the awesome snacks" ♪

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:13.567
♪ And then he hits a vape and
starts to play the alto sax ♪

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:18.601
♪ He's handing out potatoes and
some traps to catch a mouse ♪

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:22.934
♪ Let's avoid
the weird guy's house ♪

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:25.400
♪ We should find the house
that's giving

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.701
king-size candy bars ♪

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:32.234
♪ And maybe we avoid the man
that's twerking on his car ♪

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:36.567
♪ He lights off tiny fireworks
while crying on his lawn ♪

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:42.901
♪ Then he steps onto his porch
and starts to sing Celine Dion ♪

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.567
♪ He does this every year,

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:47.634
we don't know
what he's all about ♪

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:51.234
♪ Let's avoid
the weird guy's house ♪

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:52.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:57.400
-Alright, very nice!
Come on over, bud.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.267
Well done, buddy.
-Thank you. Thank you, sir.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.601
-Tom McGovern, everybody.
Give it up for Tom.

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:08.067
Now, it's time to see who won.

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.367
We're going to let our audience
decide the winner.

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:13.501
[ Drumroll ]
Yes.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:16.667
Don't be cruel, you guys.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.667
Was it Tom McGovern?

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:21.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:24.000
-Was it Allie Chipkin?

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:28.501
We're going to give it to
Tom McGovern as the winner,

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:29.634
ladies and gentlemen!

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:33.801
-Yeah!
-Nicely done.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:35.200
-Tom, congratulations.
-Yes, sir.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.434
-You get a sweatshirt that says
"I love music."

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:39.200
-Awesome.
-Congratulations.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.901
-Awesome. Thank you.
-Congratulations.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:43.067
-We're also giving you
a notebook

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:44.901
so you can write more hits.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:47.367
And in there,
we give you $1,000.

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.300
-Awesome!
-Come on.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.133
-Thank you very much.

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.167
-Happy Halloween.
-Thank you.

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:55.634
-Happy Halloween.

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:57.267
-No, no one goes home empty --
You get a sweatshirt that says

00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:58.968
"I love music," as well.

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:04.167
And you get a "Tonight Show"
notebook and $1,000, as well.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:05.667
Come on.
-Thank you.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:08.133
-Give it up for your
two new instant songwriters!

